{"name":"Crushed Out","hex":"#e0cfc8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crushed out","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of crush out"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crushed_out"}],"entries":[{"title":"Infatuation","blocks":[{"text":"Infatuation refers to being \"in love\" or intensely \"love smitten\", with possible connotations of youth, irrationality, foolishness, or capriciousness. An individual may be considered infatuated with a person they do not know well yet, or whom others view as unsuitable. In the triangular theory of love, \"infatuation\" refers to romantic passion in the absence of intimacy or commitment, as in love at first sight and limerence. A simple infatuation which is more short-lived may be referred to as a crush, or \"puppy love\" in adolescence. Infatuation might also be compared to the \"honeymoon phase\" of a relationship."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e9/Uluchi_Arujann.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infatuation","wikidata":"Q1320124"},{"title":"Puppy love","blocks":[{"text":"Puppy love, also known as a crush, is an informal term for feelings of romantic love, often felt during childhood and early adolescence. It is an infatuation often developed by one's looks and attractiveness at first sight. It is named for its resemblance to the affection that may be felt by a puppy. It is commonly associated with feelings of emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puppy_love","wikidata":"Q3226087"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg/500px-Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg/1280px-Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg/500px-Fake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Counterfeit money versus real money","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFake_100_dollar_bill_compared_to_a_real_one.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Photo_of_Albert_Ellis_on_dust_jacket.jpg/500px-Photo_of_Albert_Ellis_on_dust_jacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Photo_of_Albert_Ellis_on_dust_jacket.jpg/500px-Photo_of_Albert_Ellis_on_dust_jacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Albert Ellis c. 1966","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhoto_of_Albert_Ellis_on_dust_jacket.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.848125},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.595},{"title":"\"Forest Fires Aid the Enemy, Crush out your Cigarette\" - DPLA - f518f315ea40d3c4f903dac68d32820f","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/%22Forest_Fires_Aid_the_Enemy%2C_Crush_out_your_Cigarette%22_-_DPLA_-_f518f3